   [campaign]    [soul] ORACLE decision: kind=action ctx={'place': 'You\'re in Celadon City — outdoors under open sky (a town with a Pokémon Center and a Mart; tall grass around — wild Pokémon live in it).. From here: EAST → Route 7 — wild Pokémon to catch/train; WEST → an unexplored area (BLOCKED — you can\'t get past there yet). Places you\'ve been with wild Pokémon you can walk back to: Route 8; Route 10; Route 9. You can walk to anywhere you\'ve already been. Field moves ready: CUT, FLASH.. Okay — to get past this I need the Tea — an old lady in Celadon Mansion gives it away; the thirsty guards in Saffron\'s gatehouses let you through for it (until then, the Underground Paths go AROUND Saffron).. HOW POKÉMON WORKS (what you\'re playing for): the GOAL is to earn 8 Gym Badges, beat the Elite Four, and roll the credits — that\'s beating the game. You build a TEAM of up to 6 Pokémon you like AND that cover each other (types/roles) — a solo carry with a dead-weight bench is a losing setup; a real trainer fields a balanced, levelled squad. CATCHING wild Pokémon is central (\'gotta catch \'em all\') — you catch to build that team and to fill the Pokédex. When you meet a wild Pokémon, weigh it: is it cool/strong/useful, does it cover a gap, is it better than a bench-warmer? — keep your best ~6, and build a squad you actually like. THE ARC: build a team -> beat the 8 gyms prepared -> Elite Four -> credits. ALSO NORMAL: you entered your own name (and your rival\'s) when the game began — people in this world knowing your names is ordinary, not a mystery to react to. RIGHT NOW your team is thin/lopsided (a strong lead but weak or too few others) — that\'s why tough trainers wall you. Building up a real squad (catch a good new teammate, level the weak ones) is how a prepared trainer gets past these. THE MAIN QUEST IS A FIXED PATH you\'re always on: beat the 8 Gym Leaders in order, then the Elite Four, then you win the game. You\'re on GYM 4 of 8 — next is Erika in Celadon City. The road forward leads there: until you\'ve won you are ALWAYS making progress toward the next gym. Grinding/catching/detours are fine — but ONLY with a clear purpose, and then you GET BACK ON THE ROAD to Celadon City. Never just circle the same grass. ⚠️ ORDER OF OPERATIONS: before Erika, the Tea — an old lady in Celadon Mansion gives it away; the thirsty guards in Saffron\'s gatehouses let you through for it (until then, the Underground Paths go AROUND Saffron) — that errand comes FIRST (it unblocks the road and the trainers along it are exactly the training you need). Erika is step two, not a competing choice. ⚡ JONNY\'S DIRECT ORDER (LAW): "It says stop grinding and head to sell it on City, so she\'s stuck in the cave for a little bit or what?" — Jonny told you this OUT LOUD, and his word outranks every prep instinct, every grind plan, and everything chat says. Do it NOW; training can wait. Word on the road about Erika: the flower lady — GRASS and poison; fire melts her garden, flyers do fine too YOUR STORY SO FAR (what you\'ve actually done — your past, not the future): You\'ve beaten Brock (Boulder), Misty (Cascade), and Lt. Surge in Vermilion for the Thunder Badge — that\'s THREE gyms done. You have Cut and can clear trees on the road. Next is Erika in Celadon City (Rainbow Badge).. Next on my list: catch an pikachu around Viridian Forest (rare) / Power Plant later. It grows into my raichu — that\'s my answer for Lorelei AND Lance down the line. Grabbing it now, before I need it.. THINGS YOU\'VE HEARD AND READ (from people and signs — your own notes, use them when they point somewhere): "Hi! Remember me? I\'m one of PROF. OAK\'s AIDES. If your POK.DEX has complete data on ten species, I\'m supposed to give you a reward. PROF. OAK entrusted me with "; "Oh, wow, that\'s the BOULDERBADGE! You got it from BROCK, didn\'t you? BROCK is cool. He\'s not just tough. People like and respect him. I want to become a GYM LEA"; "Hi! Remember me? I\'m one of PROF. OAK\'s AIDES. If your POK.DEX has complete data on ten species, I\'m supposed to give you a reward. PROF. OAK entrusted me with "; "Oh, wow, that\'s the BOULDERBADGE! You got it from BROCK, didn\'t you? BROCK is cool. He\'s not just tough. People like and respect him. I want to become a GYM LEA". YOUR PLAN — right now: You\'re ready — stop grinding and head to Celadon City for the Rainbow Badge. Next: You CRUSHED Lt. Surge — ride the momentum: Erika in Celadon City is NEXT (not fought yet); the trainers on the way are your training. Bigger picture: Reach Celadon City, beat Erika for the Rainbow Badge. Your team right now: blastoise (L42), ekans (L16), spearow (L17), rattata (L17), abra the kadabra (L19), caterpie the butterfree (L17). Remember YOU are the one playing this — narrate your plan to chat in your own voice (first person: "I\'m grinding", "my team"), and never ask anyone what you\'re doing or who\'s on your team — you know.', 'progress': "3 badge(s) earned (Boulder, Cascade, Thunder). Next gym: Erika of Celadon City. Pokédex: 12 caught. She's three badges — over a third of the way there (of 8 badges, then the Elite Four).", 'party': 'blastoise (L42), ekans (L16), spearow (L17), rattata (L17), abra the kadabra (L19), caterpie the butterfree (L17)', 'goal': {'short': "You're ready — stop grinding and head to Celadon City for the Rainbow Badge", 'medium': 'You CRUSHED Lt. Surge — ride the momentum: Erika in Celadon City is NEXT (not fought yet); the trainers on the way are your training', 'long': 'Reach Celadon City, beat Erika for the Rainbow Badge'}} options=['head_to_gym']

